###############################################################################
# Q11 -- Computational resources
###############################################################################

# SevenNet-0 was trained on four A100 GPUs for 450 epochs (no time given).
# The scaling benchmarks (weak and strong scaling on up to 32 A100 GPUs,
# alpha-quartz SiO2, LAMMPS 23Jun2022) are reported as figures.

###############################################################################
# Q12 -- Gaps and ambiguities (prose; not triples)
###############################################################################

# - SevenNet is an implementation of the NequIP architecture (the paper: 'The GNN architecture of SevenNet is identical to that of NequIP'), so the models apply the registry method entity:NequIP and SevenNet is an implementation library.
# - SevenNet-0 here is the registry model SevenNet-0-MPF (trained on the M3GNet MPF data). The stub 'SevenNet-0 trained on MPtrj' evaluated by loew2025 is a later checkpoint and a different registry model.
# - The 20 SiO2 models exist to measure parallel performance; no accuracy is reported for them. Their timings (scaled-size and fixed-size tests) are figures.
# - Parameter count (0.84 million, against 16.24 million in GNoME) is in the registry label; the average-neighbour normalisation and the pruned tensor-product paths are not encoded.
# - Structural results of the Si3N4 melt-quench simulation have no MetricProperty.
# - Author affiliations are not encoded (ORCIDs are those deposited with the DOI metadata, source: crossref).

# --- BenchmarkResult labels (generated by artifacts/scripts/add_result_labels.py; do not edit) ---
<https://w3id.org/mlips/entity/result-sevennet-0-test-park2024> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "SevenNet-0 as published by Park et al. 2024 (0.84M parameters, trained on the M3GNet MPF data set) on Materials Project crystal structures over 89 elements (M3GNet MPF data set)" .
# --- end of generated BenchmarkResult labels ---
